{"title":"1989 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 1989 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b521c079f3bf8b8ae7a020f26ea4adce79d93c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2, \\ldots, 1989\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> can be expressed as the disjoint union of subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f00d48bdab1e10ace01c3130ef87a78ef2d798e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i, \\{i = 1,2, \\ldots, 117\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n</p><p>i.) each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> contains 17 elements\n</p><p>ii.) the sum of all the elements in each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is the same.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a triangle, the bisector of angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> meets the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243af6fad28c15abb3e11996374ba60e745bf543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> are defined similarly. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f0bd1bf44e9dd29cf5383c208c802b0dccb4920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> meet the lines that bisect the two external angles at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/71145755882ef0f1e12d10935523847f1692373e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce4664de7db214d4c56a42b1922cbd0fb7e7785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> similarly. Prove that the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/4/5048f2921d2acc2a714a6d6b47af71cecd32bee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0B_0C_0 = 2 \\cdot$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" /> area of hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/6/f66b7151a46075d34e8d8ea96ec594e0932516d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC_1BA_1CB_1 \\geq 4 \\cdot$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"15\" /> area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> points in the plane such that\n</p><p>i.) no three points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear, and\n</p><p>ii.) for every point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> there are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> equidistant from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3ce33ec2a34dc4fddaec3224043f4a72bbe6d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Prove that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e2599512618364e8e8a4e77ea1fec25d1fa561fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k &lt; \\frac {1}{2} + \\sqrt {2 \\cdot n}\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex quadrilateral such that the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/1445877b04adda7a099d10ed2f9f4a5f14cb8a46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, AD, BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eeed6bd9607908ea7c6936bb3b629da7f9fbbbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AD + BC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"135\" height=\"14\" /> There exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> inside the quadrilateral at a distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> from the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/1/9d199d5863b42a239b4f8f1b60b182637d5425b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = h + AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b086baf87cc7d0c818544068aa9ed497e6933d27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = h + BC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" /> Show that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce8f28be318ef82e52c506a605fb69133761ee67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {1}{\\sqrt {h}} \\geq \\frac {1}{\\sqrt {AD}} + \\frac {1}{\\sqrt {BC}}\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that for each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> there exist <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> consecutive positive integers none of which is an integral power of a prime number.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3bafe034df45c21deaf90419ec1fa9131b5539c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_{2n}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/427971afb2d5aabd3e2ed3bca718ffa26aadc29e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2, \\ldots, 2n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, is said to have property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9acb77bb66fccb38918c95b67f0a99bb3c86e2f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_i - x_{i + 1}| = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> for at least one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4d3d486e78dc1cefb3ab840b919e8fe450d8d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2, \\ldots, 2n - 1\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" /> Show that, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, there are more permutations with property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> than without.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO\" title=\"1989 IMO\">1989 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1989\">IMO 1989 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO\" title=\"1989 IMO\">1989 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO\" title=\"1988 IMO\">1988 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1989 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO\" title=\"1990 IMO\">1990 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043359\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 283/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8880/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.823      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.823      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20546:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018043359 and revision id 235233. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}